      "created_at": "2016-02-16T16:25:55.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Not sure how many people are interested, but JourneyQuest season 3 is in its last 3 days of its kickstarter. Its not looking like they are going to make it, so I figured I'd give them a quick shoutout.&nbsp;</p><p><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/zombieorpheus/journeyquest-season-3\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/zombieorpheus/journeyquest-season-3</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>These are the guys who have made The Gamers (A fun low budget movie about a bunch of people playing D&amp;D, hilarity ensues)</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSynJyq2RRo\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oSynJyq2RRo</a></p><p>The Gamers: Dorkness Rising (A much higher budget production about a new group of gamers attempting to finish their campaign, more hilarity naturally)</p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tOUksDJCijw\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tOUksDJCijw</a></p><p><span>And The Gamers: Hands of Fate (The latest chapter of the Gamers series. This one has a much stronger focus on the CCG scene)</span></p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DvlNV0riXw\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DvlNV0riXw</a></p><p><span>Not to mention JourneyQuest season 1 and 2. (A web series about a misfit group of adventurers trying to save the world. Takes place in the same world as The Gamers)</span></p><p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pVORGr2fDk8\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pVORGr2fDk8</a></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>If you like any of these consider giving the kickstarter a look.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
